02AEEBD8 5555A5C1
// one-screen camera areas: the level loader (0x00136748) gives CameraAreas authored 27.5 wide
// the screen width from 0x02AEE9E8. Keep the original 16:9 width (27.5556) there, otherwise
// every one-screen room shrinks to the 4:3 width and the camera and player get boxed in.
// Hook 0x00136A80 -> code cave 0x02138780 (unused end of .text).
00136A80 40078014
02138780 4000001C
02138784 C0F87F17
02138788 C971DC41
// fixed-position cameras (autoscrolls and scripted holds via SetAutoScrollPos; camera controller 0x006C5970, target at
// 0x006C6FD0): keep the fixed Y/Z. While the fixed X moves the camera rides it exactly like stock; once it has been still
// for 2 s (stopped or vertical scroll) X may follow the camera focus within fixed X + [0, 2*delta], so the 4:3 view
// pans inside the 16:9 frame. Room changes start on the game's position (cave G at 0x02138A00, generated below).
// StopScroll side locks (e.g. the Wonder shaft in Up 'n' Down with Puffy Lifts): the locked camera X may pan by the
// area's reach delta (cave H at 0x02138F00, hook 0x006C7BEC); boss rooms in the table use delta 0 = stock lock.
// Per-area view zoom (generator: tools/gen_zoom_v2.py, v2). The base view height G of the current area is
// written to a spare word at 0x037D1F00 by cave A and read by the view, camera-clamp and pipe-box hooks:
//   boss arenas and fixed rooms (area hashes in the table at 02138E00): Course150_Sub4 G = 21.0, delta 0;
//   Course151_Sub2, Course152_Sub4, Course153_Sub3, Course411_Course, Course415_Course, Course417_Course
//   G = 20.6667 (full 16:9 width), delta 0; Course417 artwork adjustments are awaiting play-test
//   Course411, Course415 and Course417 theater artwork adjustments are generated by tools/build_stage.py
//   small rooms (area bounds narrower than 60)  G = 15.5 (stock; huts, shops, one-screen rooms), delta 3.4444
//   wide world areas                            G = 15.75, delta 3.2778
// Cave A (0x02138800) also holds the 16:9 reach rule that used to live at 0x02138740.
// W4 Bowser Jr. (Course152_Sub4): after the opening cutscene the camera clamps to an area taller than the view and sits
// on its bottom, which the taller 4:3 view put ~2.9 blocks above stock (and the Royal Seed with it). Cave Y (0x02138D40,
// hook 0x006C66E8) gives the Y limits the stock half-height in that room only, so the camera centre matches stock, and
// with the fight zoom pins the camera at the stock height (stock never moves it vertically during the fight).
// Pinning camera Y to 3.25 expands the frustum's vertical extents to [-8.42, 14.92]; Bowser Jr.'s swim AI computes
// targets as minY + 3.0 = -5.42 (under the floor). Hook 0x01781B70 -> cave K (0x02138D88) in GetCameraBoundBox2f replaces
// minY with stock -5.50 and maxY with 12.00 so Jr.'s AI targets y = -2.50 above the floor and never gets corner-stuck.
// Debug words: 037D1F04 current area hash, 037D1F10/14 pipe-box markers, 037D1F18 delta bits,
// 037D1F1C measured area width, 037D1F20 camera controller pointer, 037D1F28 camera subject pointer. Area table at 02138E00.
